# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in real absolute host
# paths. docker compose auto-loads .env from this same directory.
#
# Add a new NAMED project (run_command, needs docker-compose-build
# capability): add a LINE here, a matching volume line in
# docker-compose.yml, and an allowlist.txt entry for any new binary
# its pipeline needs -- no code change in bash_mcp_server.py itself,
# it discovers mounted projects dynamically (see list_projects()).
LOCUSAI_DIR=/path/to/LocusAI
OPENCODE_MODEL_EVAL_DIR=/path/to/opencode-model-eval
OPENCODE_CTX_SQUID_DIR=/path/to/opencode-plugin-ctx-squid

# NOT set here, deliberately -- HOST_UID/HOST_GID, DYNAMIC_ROOT, and
# CACHE_ROOT are all computed fresh by start.sh every time the
# service launches, not stored as static values here, so none of them
# can go stale if this checkout is ever moved or launched by a
# different user later:
#   - HOST_UID/HOST_GID: `id -u`/`id -g` for whoever runs start.sh.
#     See bash_mcp_server.py's docstring ("Worker file ownership") --
#     without these, every run_in_directory() worker creates
#     host-bind-mounted files as root, not the real host user.
#   - DYNAMIC_ROOT: this checkout's own parent directory (so sibling
#     projects stay reachable via run_in_directory(), no
#     docker-compose.yml edit needed per new repo). See
#     bash_mcp_server.py's docstring for why this is read-only in the
#     coordinator (validation only) while real work happens in a
#     read-write ephemeral worker against the real host path.
#   - CACHE_ROOT: .cicd-runner-cache/ inside this checkout
#     (gitignored) -- persists npm/cargo/pip dependency-download
#     caches across separate run_in_directory() calls, instead of
#     every call re-downloading its entire dependency tree from
#     scratch. See bash_mcp_server.py's docstring ("Dependency
#     caching") for exactly what's cached and the real trade-off it
#     introduces (a global, persistent cache shared across every
#     project, not per-project or ephemeral like the rest of this
#     project's default isolation).
